age response code must be 404, but that\u2019s not what happens with the soft 404s. Also, 404 pag pages are not indexed by search engines, so they are not shown in search results. However, soft 404 error pages are indexed by crawl bots and may appear in SERPs.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/soft-404-errors\/#faq-question-1716012860591\",\"position\":3,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/soft-404-errors\/#faq-question-1716012860591\",\"name\":\"3. Explain soft 404 vs hard 404.\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The major difference between soft 404 and hard 404 is how the two are communicated to search engine crawl bots. For a regular or hard 404, the server shows a 404 error to crawl bots, while for a soft 404, the server shows a 200 OK status, so bots continue to crawl that page.\u00a0\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/soft-404-errors\/#faq-question-1716012881698\",\"position\":4,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/soft-404-errors\/#faq-question-1716012881698\",\"name\":\"4. Will fixing soft 404 errors increase the website traffic?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Once you fix the soft 404 error, the crawl bots can see more active content pages. Hence, it will index more pages and show them in SERPs, driving more website traffic.\u00a0\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/soft-404-errors\/#faq-question-1716012902496\",\"position\":5,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/soft-404-errors\/#faq-question-1716012902496\",\"name\":\"5. Does Google penalize websites for soft 404 errors?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No, there is no official penalty for a soft 404 